        'read' => 'A well-matched pair is within about 2 °C on melting temperature. A gap of five degrees or more means one primer will anneal while the other is still coming off, and the product will be weak or absent. The annealing temperature is a starting point, not a guarantee: the first few cycles of a gradient will tell you more than any formula.',
