        'check' => 'Use the Wallace rule on a primer under twenty bases: two degrees for every A or T and four for every G or C. A 19-mer with 10 GC gives about 56 °C by that rule, and the page\'s more careful estimate is usually a few degrees below it. If your hand figure is far off, count the GC content again.',
